on  Lindelof spaz series lost in which the  Looking Glass was the name of one of the  Dharma stations of the island and Andrew  Howard is playing another masked crime  fighter named Red Scare now this series  is set in Tulsa Oklahoma which might  give us a clue about this world like  maybe after the New York attacks the  American population has decided to move  away from the coast some more inland  landlocked cities that are better  protected from external threats but  Tulsa as the setting also has some  historical significance according to the  trailer footage the series also appears  to be exploring the dark history of the  1921 Tulsa race riots in which the most  prosperous black community in the  country was fire bombed and destroyed  honestly it's one of the most horrific  episodes in US history that not nearly  enough people know about but again  watchmen takes place in a fictional  history one that in the graphic novel  begins with world war two but might go  back further in history to the 20s Louis  Gossett jr. plays will Reeves who might  have some connection to that history in  the present day this fictional history  Robert Redford has been president since  1992 Redford is playing himself as  president in the series in the original  Watchmen Nixon abolished presidential  term limits and for the series a  newspaper headline shown in the trailer  suggests that Redford will not seek  another term in this America by the way  has a flag with 51 stars because in the  graphic novel after defeating Vietnam  they made Vietnam the 51st state sorry  Washington DC in Puerto Rico  dr. Manhattan is also very much part of  this story after the events of the  original Watchmen he went off world  living on Mars making plans to  experiment with life in other dimensions  in this series there's a round-the-clock  video stream of dr. Manhattan on Mars  and parades for him back on earth in the  Zack Snyder film Manhattan allows  Ozymandias to turn him into this  worldwide pariah and scapegoat him for  the New York attack though in the  graphic novel he remains an impersonal  god figure whom some worship some just  don't trust the past trailer for this  series shows him returning to Earth  clothes though this is HBO they could  probably get away with that Snyder  full-frontal but it remains unclear what  role dr. Manhattan will play in this new  series assuming society becomes too  unstable he may just come down to  intervene but with President Robert  Redford not seeking another term perhaps  dr. Manhattan will run for the office I  don't see him wanting or needing that if  only to prevent some worse alternative  now the newest trailer also features  some familiar tech - Watchmen fans the  owl ship which was night-owls batwing  thing and angela is seen wearing night  owls eyepieces suggesting the character  could return to the series or maybe  Reeves is a collector hooking her up  with his gear also one shot shows Adrian  Veidt around some steampunky looking  chamber which some are saying looks like  a time machine maybe a kind of  teleporter or maybe it's a chamber that  recreates the conditions that created  dr. Manhattan Osmond is already views  himself as a superior being a natural  step for him would be to turn himself  into a god so what are you most looking  forward to with this watchmen series  comment down below with your thoughts  follow me on twitter and instagram at  leave us and subscribe to the new rock  stars for breakdowns and theories about  everything you love thank you for  joining me and let's just hope that 24/7  coverage of dr. Manhattan on Mars is  x-rated  you can see that thing from space  [Music]

